{"title":"Ring of integers","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> be a finite <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Algebraic\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Algebraic\">algebraic</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Field_extension\" title=\"Field extension\">field extension</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/f/18faac56812975e05744319e3c6ac1016643c11b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{Q}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"16\" />. Then the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integral_closure\" title=\"Integral closure\">integral closure</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/7/2374ed8a6dc8e05a1cdad692fa5a6f2d0f0a83be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${\\mathbb{Z}}$\" width=\"11\" height=\"12\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" />, which we denote by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/2/072fcc9b727a8b6d87f18c19197404ecf30f25e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathfrak{o}_K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"11\" />, is called the <b>ring of integers</b> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" />. Rings of integers are always <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Dedekind_domain\" title=\"Dedekind domain\">Dedekind domains</a> with finite <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Class_number&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Class number (page does not exist)\">class numbers</a>.\n</p><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Ring_of_integers&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018003440\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.009 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.014 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 25/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 289/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1031/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.786      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.786      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3303:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018003440 and revision id 228529. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}